'Ring of Nestor' in the context of Aegean forgeries and authenticity debates. By
revisiting key iconographic features and comparisons, the paper aims to 
contribute to the ongoing discourse regarding the ring's significance in Minoan 
and Mycenaean art. 1. The text explores the authenticity of the 'Ring of Nestor'
through iconographic analysis. 3. The connection between incurved altars and the
ring's depiction supports its authenticity. 5. Generations of scholars have 
debated the genuineness of both Nestor's and Minos' rings. Any a priori 
disqualification of such a vast resource of emerging data is to ignore an 
