Ring of Nestor, noting that debates have largely centered on iconography. It 
evaluates arguments against the ring’s antiquity and considers stylistic, 
iconographic, and technical aspects within the broader context of Aegean glyptic
art. The study revisits Evans’s and later interpretations, discusses suspicions 
of modern forgery, and examines features such as the depiction of altars, trees,
guardian creatures, and human figures, as well as craftsmanship and production 
techniques, to assess whether the ring is ancient. The DOI provides a stable 
