published in ANNUARIO della Scuola Archeologica di Atene e delle Missioni 
Italiane in Oriente. The article analyzes the iconography of the Ring of Nestor 
in the broader context of Aegean forgeries and authenticity debates. It reviews 
key iconographic features and comparative material, explores contradictions in 
technical analyses in Aegean studies, and argues that the depiction of incurved 
altars on the ring supports its authenticity. Eliopoulos notes longstanding 
debates over the genuineness of both Nestor’s and Minos’ rings and stresses the 
importance of accessible reference material for finger rings. The study compares
motifs such as altars, trees, and guardians on the Ring of Nestor with other 
